 "answer": "The environment variable is `OLLAMA_MODELS`. On Windows, you set it in your user account, and it changes where Ollama stores downloaded models instead of the default home directory. \"Edit or create a new variable for your user account for `OLLAMA_MODELS` where you want the models stored\" [ollama/docs/windows.md].\n\nQuit and relaunch Ollama after saving so it picks up the new value. \"If Ollama is already running, Quit the tray application and relaunch it from the Start menu, or a new terminal started after you saved the environment variables.\" [ollama/docs/windows.md]",
